    {
      "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@109155",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "GLOUCESTER.\nAlack, alack, Edmund, I like not this unnatural dealing. When I desired their leave that I might pity him, they took from me the use of mine own house; charged me on pain of perpetual displeasure, neither to speak of him, entreat for him, or any way sustain him.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@109155/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 11,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@109155/line-2",
          "start": 12,
          "end": 274,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 3282610,
        "end": 3282915,
        "line": 119751,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap18/p@109155",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_18.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "GLOUCESTER.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 11
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@109464",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "EDMUND.\nMost savage and unnatural!",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@109464/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@109464/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 34,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 3282919,
        "end": 3282983,
        "line": 119758,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap18/p@109464",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_18.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "EDMUND.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@109532",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "GLOUCESTER.\nGo to; say you nothing. There is division between the Dukes, and a worse matter than that: I have received a letter this night;—’tis dangerous to be spoken;—I have locked the letter in my closet: these injuries the King now bears will be revenged home; there’s part of a power already footed: we must incline to the King. I will look him, and privily relieve him: go you and maintain talk with the Duke, that my charity be not of him perceived: if he ask for me, I am ill, and gone to bed. If I die for it, as no less is threatened me, the King my old master must be relieved. There is some strange thing toward, Edmund; pray you be careful.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@109532/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 11,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@109532/line-2",
          "start": 12,
          "end": 653,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
