    {
      "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.3/p@110266",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "EDMUND.\nThis courtesy, forbid thee, shall the Duke\nInstantly know; and of that letter too.\nThis seems a fair deserving, and must draw me\nThat which my father loses, no less than all:\nThe younger rises when the old doth fall.",
